SUMMARY:Advanced B Ride (16-18mph) - Final Ride of\n2026 - LC New Holland 
 Reservoir (39R)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nBe Safe\, Have Fun\, and 
 Ride Together\nRide leader: Dave Evans\nAnticipated Average Pace: (16-18 m
 ph)\nRoute: https://ridewithgps.com/routes/27221023\nNOTE 10 AM START TIME
 ! This is an Advanced B ride. The ride leader will ride at the advertised 
 average speed. This is intended to be a group ride with a no-drop rule as 
 the main goal. The ride leader will do his/her best to keep the group toge
 ther with occasional regroupings and/or splitting into multiple groups to 
 align to pace capabilities.\nPlease do not join this ride if you are not w
 illing to ride with the group. If you exceed the posted pace\, you will be
  riding by yourself and encouraged to join a faster group. If maintaining 
 a 16-18 mph average is beyond your current ability level\, please consider
  joining a slower ride first.\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. Please b
 ring water and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inf
 lator).\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require L
 BC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on Meetu
 p does not mean you are a club member. Join here [Member Signup](https://w
 ww.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nYour RSV
 P is your agreement to abide by the club's [Code of Conduct](https://www.l
 ancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=3239
 84)\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lancasterb
 ikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
