BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adult-services-program-200759"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Marching to Independence: Lancaster Soldiers at the Battle of Fort
  Lee
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T194500
UID:8b4ae437d7d379c1aa4f3660253d2739@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nHow did ordinar
 y men from Lancaster County end up on the front lines of the American Revo
 lution? Step back in time with living historian Samuel Leamer to uncover t
 he harrowing story of Clotz's Battalion-- part of the legendary "Flying Ca
 mp" mobile reserve.Relive the tension of November 1776 at the Battle of Fo
 rt Lee\, discover the courageous stories of local soldiers fighting for a 
 brand-new nation\, and see how modern historians uncover the past to keep 
 their legacy alive. Don't miss this immersive journey into the fight for i
 ndependence!Registration is encouraged!A Berks County native and Cairn Uni
 versity history graduate\, Presenter Sam Leamer has spent a lifetime bring
 ing the past to life through reenactments-- and a decade mastering the art
  of modern coffee. By blending historical scholarship with coffee expertis
 e\, Sam offers a richer\, deeper look into Colonial Coffee Culture\, showi
 ng how the humble coffee bean helped fuel America’s fight for independen
 ce.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adult-services-prog
 ram-200759
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
