BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/yiddish-concert-200986"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Klezmer and Jewish Music by members of Quartet Harriet: Christophe
 r Brooks\, violin and Laurie Reese\, violoncello
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T193000
UID:03dd90ef59def93abe6383a94f467c00@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Music\, Everyone\n\nJoin us for an evening of Klezmer and Jewi
 sh music. Klezmer music is traditional instrumental music of the Ashkenazi
  Jews. Meet the musicians\; Christopher Brooks was born and raised in Broo
 klyn\, New York. He began studying the violin at PS 8 in Brooklyn Heights 
 and at the Third Street Music School. Attending the New School of Music in
  Philadelphia\, Mr. Brooks studied violin with Jascha Brodsky and Geoffrey
  Michaels. He has played chamber music and been a member of numerous orche
 stras. Laurie Haines Reese is a cellist dedicated to creating and performi
 ng music—especially new music—that explores the cello’s creative pos
 sibilities. An accomplished classical musician with a lifelong curiosity a
 bout what else the cello can do\, she is equally at home in folk\, jazz\, 
 improvisatory\, and experimental music. Based in Lancaster\, PA\, Laurie h
 as freelanced and concertized extensively throughout the United States and
  Europe.This performance is made possible through a grant from the Yiddish
  Book Center. Yiddish Book Center
LOCATION:Lititz\, LTZ Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/yiddish-concert-200986
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
