X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Victorian Christmas: Customs & Costumes
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261215T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261215T194500
UID:4441d64306f0c760b525b5a531acddbc@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nStep back in time and disco
 ver how many of our favorite holiday traditions began! Join historian Lynn
 ette Miller from Landis Valley for a fascinating look into the holiday cus
 toms\, festive decorations\, and seasonal fashions of the Victorian era.Fr
 om decorated evergreen trees and handmade gifts to period-appropriate wint
 er attire\, this presentation explores how Victorian-era families celebrat
 ed the holiday season. The presentation will be followed by a Q&A session 
 with the audience.Free and open to the public. Registration is requested.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/victorian-christmas-cust
 oms-costumes-202541
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
