SUMMARY:The Neverland Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270107T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270107T193000
UID:a59030a4ec84787bbff50106d8ad318b@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nThe book club where our readin
 g tastes never grow up! Every month\, we'll discuss one middle-grade or yo
 ung adult book. Here are just a few of the reasons to join:  - Short books
  (easier to read before book club!)  - Revisiting nostalgic stories or fin
 ding new favorites  - Discussing meaningful topics and themes (you might b
 e surprised by how deep children's literature can get!)Registration is enc
 ouraged\, but walk-ins are welcome!Reading List:   January 7: Bridge to Te
 rabithia by Katherine Paterson   February 4: Roll of Thunder\, Hear My Cry
  by Mildred D. Taylor   March 4: Redwall by Brian Jacques   April 1: Speak
  by Laurie Halse Anderson   May 6: The Outsiders by S. E. Hinton   June 3:
  Matilda by Roald Dahl   July 1: Holes by Louis Sachar   August 5: Looking
  for Alaska by John Green   September 2: A Wrinkle in Time by Madeleine L'
 Engle   October 7: The Giver by Lois Lowry   November 4: The Secret Garden
  by Frances Hodgson Burnett   December 2: Charlotte's Web by E. B. White T
 his is a book club for adults (ages 18+) to discuss children's books. For 
 a list of children's programs at LPL\, please check our events calendar.
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Board Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/neverland-book-club-2046
 94
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
